.TH "GIT\-PSYKOREBASE" "1" "August 2021" "" "Git Extras"
.SH "NAME"
\fBgit\-psykorebase\fR \- Rebase a branch with a merge commit
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBgit psykorebase\fR [\-h|\-\-help]
.br
\fBgit psykorebase\fR <target_branch> [<feature_branch>] [\-\-no\-ff]
.br
\fBgit psykorebase\fR \-\-continue
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Rebase the \fBfeature_branch\fR on top of the \fBtarget_branch\fR, the \fBfeature_branch\fR defaults to the current one\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.IP
Show usage information\.
.P
\fB\-\-no\-ff\fR
.IP
Force a commit message even if there are no conflicts\.
.P
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-continue\fR
.IP
Continue the rebase after conflicts have been resolved\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Complete rebase of a feature branch on top of main with merge commit:
.P
Setup:
.IP "" 4
.nf
$ git checkout \-b feature main
$ echo "feature change" > feature\.txt
$ git add feature\.txt && git commit \-m "Add feature"
$ git checkout main
$ echo "main change" > main\.txt
$ git add main\.txt && git commit \-m "Update main"
$ git checkout feature
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Command:
.IP "" 4
.nf
$ git psykorebase main \-\-no\-ff
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Output:
.IP "" 4
.nf
Rebasing feature on top of main
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
State verification:
.IP "" 4
.nf
$ git rev\-parse \-\-abbrev\-ref HEAD
feature
$ git log \-1 \-\-pretty=%s
Psycho\-rebased branch feature on top of main
$ test \-f feature\.txt && test \-f main\.txt && echo "State verified"
State verified
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Handle conflicts:
.IP "" 4
.nf
$ git add README\.md
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Continue rebase:
.IP "" 4
.nf
$ git psykorebase \-\-continue
.fi
.IP "" 0
